pull_request.body:
This follow-up revises the flow after the Naur-first opening.

The article now:
- introduces the research object as the whole automated software-development system before asking the question;
- names model weights, prompts, code, runtime, tools, persistence, and checks as jointly producing behavior;
- asks the central question once, in terms of an automated software factory and delayed feedback;
- separates the research-program claim from the system-boundary explanation instead of placing both in one abrupt paragraph;
- broadens the learning surface from programs, rules, schemas, and tests to weight updates, prompt and retained-state revisions, code and tool changes, and runtime policy;
- defines theory mediation after the general system-learning path;
- combines the neighboring-system discussion and removes the later restatement of the question;
- improves the transition into the two testbeds; and
- aligns the functional table with the established weight-plus-prompt model-mediated operation.

It also adds the Naur ingest to `source_notes`, since the opening now relies directly on the original essay.
